Package: benchmarkreliability
Title: Benchmarks as Measurement Instruments: Signal, Noise, and Rank Stability
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Michael", "Hardy", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Analysis code for "Benchmarks as Measurement Instruments:
    Quantifying Signal and Noise for More Efficient AI Evaluations Under
    Distribution Shift". Recasts AI benchmark reliability as a signal-to-noise
    ratio from a crossed random-effects variance decomposition, maps variance
    components to expected rank concordance, introduces the lambda*_6
    item-level reliability proxy for the many-items/few-models regime, and
    evaluates reliability under positive distribution shift of the evaluated
    model population.
